    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0388" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/231a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Spain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-20T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 20, 1916, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>197. Following message to you from Ambassador Willard:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>In relation to the communication which the President has sent to the
                        belligerent nations, and of which a copy has been sent you for delivery to
                        the Spanish <pb facs="0389" n="103" xml:id="pg103"/> Government, I am
                        directly authorized by the President to cable that you may say to His
                        Majesty’s Government that, having the same end in view, the time seems
                        opportune for that Government to act, and, if willing, to support the
                        position taken by this Government.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
